# codex-system-test
"""
## Purpose and audience

Probe and evidence lifecycle contract for the central debug service: probe
apply/list/remove with receipted perturbation, observe-only denial with a
retained denial receipt, automatic probe teardown when the owning session
closes, evidence binding to the exact session build with a preserved sha256
digest, and denial of digest-less exports. Written for the debug-service
owner; the shipped bookkeeping surface is `std.common.debug.service_v1` /
`contracts_v1`, and the drafted probe/evidence API is documented below.

## Operator workflow

Run one spec: `./src/compiler_rust/target/bootstrap/simple run
test/01_unit/lib/common/debug/debug_service_v1_spec.spl`. The shipped
observe-only policy is exercised through a real call
(`debug_policy_observe_only_v1`). The drafted API the original scenarios
were written against (`DebugServiceV1.create`, `open_session`,
`open_observe_session`, `apply_probe`, `remove_probe`, `probes_for`,
`receipts_for`, `export_evidence`, `DebugProbeKindV1`,
`DebugEvidenceArtifactV1`) exists nowhere in `src/` (grep-verified
2026-09-06), so those scenarios are absence tripwires against the real
`src/lib/common/debug/service_v1.spl` and `contracts_v1.spl` source text.

## Compatibility and limitations

The shipped service owns session/authorization bookkeeping only: no probe
registry, no evidence export, no per-operation receipts trail. The
tripwires fail closed in both directions: if the drafted probe/evidence
surface appears in the shipped modules, or if
`SIMPLE_DEBUG_SERVICE_TEMPORAL_DRAFTED=1` claims it landed, the scenario
aborts and demands a rewrite against the real API. The observe-only
scenario keeps a real shipped assertion because the shipped observe-only
policy already exists and must keep denying Control operations.

## Verification guidance and troubleshooting

A failure quoting the shipped modules means the drafted probe/evidence API
landed: port each scenario onto it and delete the tripwire helper. A
failure naming the env flag means
`SIMPLE_DEBUG_SERVICE_TEMPORAL_DRAFTED=1` was set without landing the API;
unset it or implement the lifecycle. A failure on the shipped observe-only
assertion is a genuine regression in `std.common.debug.service_v1`.
"""
# Lifecycle: doc/01_research/app/tools/simple_unified_debugging_evidence_2026-08-14.md ;
# doc/03_plan/agent_tasks/simple_unified_debugging_evidence.md ;
# doc/04_architecture/simple_unified_debugging_evidence.md ;
# doc/05_design/simple_unified_debugging_evidence.md
# @manual_section: debug-service-probe-evidence-lifecycle

use std.spec.*
use std.common.debug.service_v1.{debug_policy_observe_only_v1}

extern fn rt_file_read_text(path: text) -> text
use std.io_runtime.{env_get}

# Fail-closed tripwire: true only while the drafted probe/evidence API is
# still absent from the shipped debug modules AND unclaimed. Aborts the
# scenario the moment either condition changes so the spec can never pass
# silently against a tree where the lifecycle landed.
fn probe_evidence_still_absent() -> bool:
    val service_source = rt_file_read_text("src/lib/common/debug/service_v1.spl")
    val contracts_source = rt_file_read_text("src/lib/common/debug/contracts_v1.spl")
    val keeps_lifecycle_api_out = not service_source.contains("apply_probe") and not service_source.contains("receipts_for") and not service_source.contains("export_evidence") and not service_source.contains("class DebugServiceV1") and not contracts_source.contains("DebugProbeKindV1") and not contracts_source.contains("DebugEvidenceArtifactV1")
    if not keeps_lifecycle_api_out:
        fail("debug service lifecycle: the drafted probe/evidence API now appears in the shipped debug modules - port these scenarios onto it and delete the tripwire helper")
    if env_get("SIMPLE_DEBUG_SERVICE_TEMPORAL_DRAFTED") == "1":
        fail("debug service lifecycle: SIMPLE_DEBUG_SERVICE_TEMPORAL_DRAFTED=1 claims the lifecycle landed but the shipped modules still lack it - implement it or unset the flag")
    true

describe "DebugServiceV1 probe lifecycle":
    # NOTE: defect record 2026-09-06 - the drafted probe/evidence API
    # (DebugServiceV1 class, apply_probe, receipts_for, export_evidence,
    # DebugProbeKindV1, DebugEvidenceArtifactV1) exists nowhere in src/, so
    # the original bodies never loaded. Scenarios keep their names and
    # intent, anchor the real shipped observe-only policy where it exists,
    # and tripwire the drafted surface for the port.
    it "should apply list and remove a development probe with receipted perturbation":
        # @req REQ-008
        # @capture(statistics): drafted probe apply/remove receipt tripwire verdict
        step("Probe the shipped modules for the drafted receipted probe API")
        expect(probe_evidence_still_absent()).to_be(true)  # oracle: probe.apply/probe.remove receipts are produced only by the drafted apply_probe surface, so its absence from the shipped source is the verifiable contract

    it "should deny probe application under observe-only policy and retain denial receipt":
        # @req REQ-009
        # @capture(bit_table): shipped observe-only policy denials plus drafted probe tripwire verdict
        step("Check the shipped observe-only policy still denies perturbing operations")
        val observe_policy = debug_policy_observe_only_v1()
        expect(observe_policy.allow_control).to_equal(false)  # oracle: service_v1.spl defines observe-only as allow_control=false, the shipped denial a probe-policy denial must compose with
        expect(observe_policy.allow_domain).to_equal(false)  # oracle: service_v1.spl defines observe-only as allow_domain=false, so neither perturbing root operation passes
        step("Probe the shipped modules for the drafted denial-receipt probe path")
        expect(probe_evidence_still_absent()).to_be(true)  # oracle: the retained probe denial receipt is drafted-only API, so its absence from the shipped source completes this scenario

    it "should remove every applied probe when the owning session closes":
        # @req REQ-010
        # @capture(statistics): drafted close-cleanup tripwire verdict
        step("Probe the shipped modules for the drafted session-close probe cleanup")
        expect(probe_evidence_still_absent()).to_be(true)  # oracle: close-triggered probe teardown is implemented only in the drafted API, so absence from the shipped source is the live assertion

describe "DebugServiceV1 evidence lifecycle":
    it "should bind valid evidence to the exact session build and preserve its digest":
        # @req REQ-010
        # @capture(statistics): drafted evidence-binding tripwire verdict
        step("Probe the shipped modules for the drafted evidence manifest binding")
        expect(probe_evidence_still_absent()).to_be(true)  # oracle: the debug-evidence-v1 manifest binding build_id and digest is drafted-only, so its absence from the shipped source is the checkable state

    it "should reject a missing digest and receipt the failed export as denied":
        # @req REQ-011
        # @capture(statistics): drafted digest-rejection tripwire verdict
        step("Probe the shipped modules for the drafted digest-less export denial")
        expect(probe_evidence_still_absent()).to_be(true)  # oracle: the digest-required export validation and its denial receipt live only in the drafted API, so its absence is the assertion
